# Target C: all-small-curvature M=5 one-deficit packet and a profile-flexible root

Date: 2026-10-07. Authority: main `4b0b982451effe3e8183edfce349ce4c25f9a3bb`,
state `2026-10-07.audit.74`. **Proved candidate awaiting independent audit**
for the M=5 family and the root lemma below. No canonical self-promotion.
C-II and Level I remain open.

## 1. The M=5 one-deficit family is excluded

For every sufficiently small positive curvature in the specified M=5
six-direction unit wall, there is a strict N=61-site packet after deletion
of wall vertex (1,4). Thus an arbitrary canonical old interior cloud with
z=N-1=60 points yields a contact-loss contradiction. The old points have
no assumed lattice, contact or vacancy structure.

The proof follows the independently certified construction in
`target_c_one_deficit_all_small_curvature_M4_2026-10-07.md`: start with the
descending-rate sorting chart, remove target site (1,3), strictly open every
remaining auxiliary contact, then add the inward root. Every deleted old
interior label and the deleted wall label is paid. No new contact or unit
triangle is introduced. The canonical one-vertex shield retains all outside
isolates; strict containment gives every new upper constraint. At least two
old contacts disappear. This is the audit.64 endpoint, not a new normal-form
assumption.

The new M=5 basis has 121 moving/eta columns and gives positive leading
coefficients on *all* 146 exact unit rows for t=tan(theta/2)>0 sufficiently
small. Leading orders range from zero through seven; every tracked
remainder order is at least 19. All 3829 inactive wall-plus-chart pairs have
positive leading squared-distance gaps. The exact unit-support identity is
checked independently by coefficients of the complex unit factors.

Inputs: `research/target_c_one_deficit_opening_basis_M5_2026_10_07.json`.
Run `python3 research/verify_target_c_one_deficit_symbolic_opening_2026_10_07.py 5`.
Output: `research/target_c_one_deficit_symbolic_opening_M5_certificate_2026_10_07.json`.
The basis was found by an exact Q(sqrt(3)) simplex search at t=1/10000,
not by accepting a floating near-zero margin. An independent full finite
endpoint at that parameter is in the strict-root packet certificate.
The positive Laurent coefficients, not that one sample, prove the
all-small-curvature statement.

Simply transporting a floating-discovered basis from a larger angle
failed an exact leading row. That failed *basis* is not an impossibility
result for the packet. The exact replacement basis resolves the scope gap.

## 2. A root lemma for arbitrary strictly ordered symmetric rate profiles

The following broadens the arithmetically spaced root calculation without
assuming a general opening theorem.

Let M>=3 and let a_0>a_1>...>a_(M-1) be any fixed strictly decreasing
symmetric real rate list: a_(M-1-h)=-a_h. Put A=a_0>0 and
Delta=a_0-a_1>0. Symmetry implies a_1>=0 for M>=3, so Delta<=A.
Construct the six-sided wall by sorting exp(i a_h theta) along each side,
and its descending-prefix sorting interior. For sufficiently small theta>0
this is a strictly convex unit-separated unit wall with corner radius
L(theta)=sum cos(a_h theta), and the sorting chart is unit-separated.
Omit target h=(1,M-2), and let v be wall vertex (1,M-1). With
w=v_basis-u_basis, define

`r=exp(i(a_0+a_1)theta/2) w`,
`root=v+3 sin(Delta theta/2) Jr`.

**Lemma.** For every sufficiently small positive theta, this root lies
strictly inside the wall and is strictly more than one from every
remaining wall/chart site other than the omitted target and old v.

*Neighbour clearance.* The two adjacent wall tangents have angles
(a_0-Delta)theta and a_0 theta relative to w, so exact squared root
clearances to both wall neighbours are

`1+3 sin^2(Delta theta/2)>1`.

The only remaining limiting interior unit neighbour is x=(0,M-1).
The first velocities are

`v'=-A Jw`, `x'=A Jv_basis`,
`root'=(3Delta/2-A)Jw`.

Since v(0)-x(0)=u_basis, its half-squared-distance derivative is

`(sqrt(3)/2)(2A-3Delta/2)>0`,

using Delta<=A. The omitted target has velocity A Ju_basis, and its
corresponding derivative would be -3sqrt(3)Delta/4<0. Every other pair
has strict limiting distance above one, so no further blocker is omitted.

*Every wall support line.* Write b_j=a_(M-1-j) for the ascending wall
rates and alpha_j=sum_(h<j)b_h. The edge-j first containment coefficient
from its initial endpoint to the root is

`3Delta/2-A-alpha_j-b_j(M-1-j)`.

Because b_h>=b_j for h=j,...,M-2,

`alpha_j+b_j(M-1-j) <= sum_(h=0)^(M-2) b_h=-A`.

The coefficient is therefore at least 3Delta/2>0, including j=M-1.
At zero the root is in the relative interior of this wall side, so every
other side has strict limiting containment. Hence the root is inside
the actual convex wall. All claims are fixed-profile, sufficiently-small-
curvature statements, with no uniform onset or generic-container premise.

Consequently *any* strict opening of the descending sorting chart with
this one boundary-row vacancy can be converted into the N-site full-source
exchange, even for these nonuniform symmetric profiles. The role of the
root is now separated from the harder simultaneous-opening theorem.
This flexibility is available for parameter discovery or chamber transfer;
it does not itself supply either.

## 3. Exact search and remaining quantified obligation

`research/discover_target_c_exact_one_deficit_opening_2026_10_07.py` implements
exact finite Q(sqrt(3)) primal simplex on all actual unit rows of the
specified chart, with velocity coordinates bounded by one. A positive
output gives exact opening derivatives only. A fully checked dual gives
nonexistence of strict opening only at that precise auxiliary packet.
Iteration limits give no mathematical nonexistence claim. Finite amplitude,
all inactive pairs, root clearance, full-source shielding and universal
parameter continuation remain separate obligations; the two verifiers
above supply them for the listed M=4,5 results.

The still-missing wall theorem is an all-M construction or induction for
one-deficit opening, especially as M becomes macroscopic. M=4 and M=5
are quantified curvature families, not an unbounded population family.
Canonical audit.74 localizes z=N clouds but does not exclude them at
finite curvature. Arbitrary actual chamber extraction, paired exterior-
cap/core release and full-core face-coupled finite motion remain open.
The exact M=6 search continues; no outcome is claimed before its certificate.
